WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.535
-Oh, it's so good
to be out of my house.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.536
[ Laughter ]
-I mean, with a full audience.

00:00:04.536 --> 00:00:06.305
How's that feel? Come on.
-Oh, my God, it feels so good.

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:08.073
I didn't know how much
I needed it.

00:00:08.073 --> 00:00:10.744
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah. Right? We need it.

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:12.144
I want to get into the book,

00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:14.647
but I have a bigger thing
I want to talk to you about.

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:18.217
This is very exciting for me
because I --

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:20.252
This is real.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:21.554
Oh, we're going in.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:22.855
-We're going to go in.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:25.225
You had an experience
with a UFO.

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.793
-Yes, I did.

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.094
I did. Yes.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.796
-Walk me through it.

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.630
Did you know that you were going
to have this experience?

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.800
-I did not know,
as many people don't.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.068
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:39.438
But, yeah, so I am a huge alien,
paranormal conspiracist.

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:40.840
It's my hobby.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.875
I love that more than anything
else in the world.

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:45.110
And I was just -- I was
in the middle of Hollywood

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.480
and I was walking down
Santa Monica Boulevard.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.815
-Nighttime, daytime?
-Daytime.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.449
Middle of the day.
-Daytime UFO?

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:52.652
-Daytime. Daytime UFO, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:56.423
And so I just saw this thing
hovering in the sky

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:57.890
and I remember looking up
thinking like,

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.626
"This can't be real." Like, "I
want this too much." You know?

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:02.962
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:04.363
You're like, "Yeah, come on."

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:08.435
-So I whipped out my camera
and it was like a cylinder shape

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.269
and it was not moving
with the wind.

00:01:10.269 --> 00:01:12.772
It was moving kind of like --
almost like a dog's tail.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:16.843
Just like this, just hovering,
several hundred feet above me.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:19.612
-This is a UFO.
So, say that's a UFO.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.181
-Okay, I'm trying to do this --
This is gonna look phallic.

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:25.718
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.320
-Alright.
-Basically like this.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.188
-So it's that?
-Yeah. Am I turning you on?

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:31.023
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:32.625
-But, wait, so it's not
this way?

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:35.328
-It was not this way. No, no.
It was --

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.030
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.197
-Sorry, get your mind
out of the --

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:39.465
-It was happy to see me.

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:42.168
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.537
-We're talking about UFOs here.
-Yeah.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.606
-So it's like almost
missile-like.

00:01:47.606 --> 00:01:49.342
-Missile -- yes, that's a great
way of putting it, yeah.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.977
And it was very --
it wasn't a balloon

00:01:51.977 --> 00:01:54.213
because it was very
bottom-heavy, like myself.

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:56.816
[ Laughter ]
-Give me that. Give me that.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:02:00.686
-Yeah, so I caught a video of it
and, yeah, I think we have it.

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:03.088
-Chris brought the video.
This is unbelievable.

00:02:03.088 --> 00:02:05.624
This is real footage of
Chris Colfer's UFO sighting.

00:02:05.624 --> 00:02:06.993
Take a look at this.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.931
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.599
-I see it.
-There it is.

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:18.237
Wait. I see this.
-I mean --

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:21.006
Very creepy.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:22.374
Yeah. So I think -- Yeah.

00:02:22.374 --> 00:02:24.477
[ Applause ]
Thank you. Yeah.

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:26.045
-That's wild that you saw it,

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:29.182
and you thought enough
to bring your phone out.

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:31.684
-Right, right. And I sent it
to everyone I knew and, like,

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.586
you would have thought
I won like a Pulitzer,

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:36.556
because everyone was like,
"Oh, Chris, congratulations.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.625
You've been working for this
for so long."

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:39.892
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:41.927
-It finally happened!

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:44.731
-God has a plan. God has a plan.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.632
-"God has a plan."

00:02:46.632 --> 00:02:49.101
And I believe it.
I believe it was a UFO.

00:02:49.101 --> 00:02:52.438
I want to talk about your book,
"A Tale of Sorcery."

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.373
This is your 18th book.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:56.142
-Congrats on these.
How much time --

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:59.078
They take up all of your --
This is years of work.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.446
-Yeah.

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.248
-And do you have, like,
deadlines you have to get to?

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.183
-Lot of deadlines, yeah.

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:05.618
And yeah, no, it is
a lot of work

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.353
and it requires so much
self-discipline.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:10.723
And I think --
I'm wrapping up --

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:13.192
It's a trilogy,
and I'm wrapping up the trilogy,

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:14.793
and I think I'm ending it
on a nice spot.

00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:17.363
So I think I'm going to
take a little bit of a break

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:20.300
from writing and just,
you know, let the muscle

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.201
kind of relax a little bit.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:25.271
And also, like,
this weird thing happened.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:28.708
I was at a bar,
and this man came over

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.676
and just started
flirting with me.

00:03:30.676 --> 00:03:33.946
Like aggressively flirting with
me and offered to get me a drink

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:36.482
and all this stuff,
and I politely declined

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.918
because I'm taken and he was
like, "Oh, that's okay.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:41.821
By the way, I loved your books
when I was a kid."

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:45.557
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.557 --> 00:03:49.662
And I said, I said,
"Okay, that's not possible

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:52.865
because the first one came out
nine years ago

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:55.268
and that would have made you --"
and he goes, "11."

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.370
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.971
-Wow.
-And it was really traumatic,

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:00.506
so I think I'm going to
take a little break.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:03.342
[ Laughter and applause ]
Yeah.

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:05.111
-That spooked you.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:07.313
You go, "That's it. I'm done.
I got to take a little break."

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.215
I understand. I understand.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:10.449
-But these are great books.

00:04:10.449 --> 00:04:12.485
I mean, you got to be --

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.187
You have to be proud of
what you've done.

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:16.589
-Oh, thank you. Yeah, I am.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.157
And I know, like,
a lot of people told me

00:04:19.157 --> 00:04:22.561
I could never do this
because of who and what I was.

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:25.932
So I am very proud that
I'm able to show kids

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:29.835
that someone like us,
someone like me can do it,

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:31.904
and I'm really proud of

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:34.340
how many other kids
I've inspired to write,

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.043
because I know how therapeutic
writing was for me growing up,

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:40.212
and it was a constant escape
whenever you needed one.

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:41.847
So, yeah, I'm really happy

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:44.250
I'm encouraging kids
to put pen to paper.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.652
-On behalf of all the parents,
thanks for doing all this stuff.

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:47.786
We love these books.
-Oh, thank you so much.

00:04:47.786 --> 00:04:48.988
-Read!
-Thank you.

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.089
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.490
-Get your kids
out there reading.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.658
Chris Colfer, everybody!

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:56.428
"A Tale of Sorcery"
is available now.

00:04:56.428 --> 00:04:57.597
It's out today.

